# Build and install with Polyscreen

Never use `flutter install`, `adb uninstall`, or `adb install` without `-r`. `flutter install` uninstalls first and deletes local measurements (`bp.db`, settings).

When the user asks to install on a phone or emulator:

1. Build from the repository root with FVM. Do not start a long-running `flutter run`.

```bash
fvm flutter build apk --debug
```

APK path: `build/app/outputs/flutter-apk/app-debug.apk`

2. List devices with Polyscreen `mobile_devices_list`. Use the exact serial. Prefer the physical phone the user has been using. Do not guess when several devices are connected.

3. Install with Polyscreen `mobile_app_install`:
   - `path`: the APK above (absolute)
   - `replace`: `true` (in-place update; keeps data)
   - never set uninstall-only or skip replace

4. If they want it opened, `mobile_app_launch` with `packageName` `com.shenepoy.janan.debug` (debug APK) and `displayId` `0`. Release installs stay `com.shenepoy.janan`.

Rebuild before install when source is newer than the APK. If replace fails because of a signature mismatch, stop and tell the user — do not uninstall to force it.